# The mapping's own bytes are written by the test's writer threads while the
# flusher copies them out. That is the design: the barrier reports WHICH
# bytes changed, and Vulkan makes the application responsible for not
# writing memory a submit is consuming. Suppressed so the run can answer
# the question it exists for, which is whether the barrier's own metadata
# still races.
race:mapped_write_barrier_test.cpp
